---Creates a string containing the provided arguments based on the specified format string.
---
---Format String: Formatting a value is done by specifying `{}` as part of the format string, or `{<options>}` where
---`<options>` varies based on the type being formatted. Positional argument formatting can also be done via `{<argument
---number>}` where `{0}` represents the first argument, `{1}` the second and so on. See fmtlib for more information on
---the available format string options.
---
---Warning: Only elementary types (numbers, strings, booleans, and nil) are supported. Other types, such as tables and
---functions, get formatted as the underlying type name where available.
---@param format string String representing the desired output format.
---@param ... any Values to format.
---@return string # Formatted output obtained based on the provided format string and arguments.
